  "term": "midpoint",
  "definition": "In this source, midpoint refers to an enzyme acting in the middle of the kynurenine pathway rather than at its end. Specifically, kynurenine-3-monooxygenase is described as a midpoint enzyme because it functions between upstream and downstream pathway metabolites.",
